>>
endobj
403 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This model is what i define as my A+ bread and butter, always terminating my trading session before 10am. Quick in and out and easy to spot providing on average 80 -120 pts, it usually presents two distinct trade opportunities, the judas trades from 9:30 to the reversal window and the actual reversal trade between the 9:40 and 9:50.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
404 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1245 0 R
/E (Trade #1 )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
405 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (As stated above, this model presents two trades with two levels of difficulty, the first trade is where we position ourselves right at the open where we participate in the judas move \(false breakout\) towards the projections of the range where the reversal will take place.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
406 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The time window of this trade spans from 9:30 open until the 9:40 -9:50 reversal window where the real move will happen. I suggest to have positions closed as we reach the reversal window, the yield of this trade outcome will vary depending on the size of the 6-9 range \(e.g. the distances from open to projection levels\) application of risk to reward needs to be considered\))
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
407 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1246 0 R
/E (Trade #2)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
408 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The second trade in this model is easier to trade, filters out the volatility of the open and allows you to let price develop before taking place in any position avoiding to be knocked out of your trade.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
409 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Here is where we participate in the reversal during the 9:40 - 9:50 window, levels of interest will be the mean reversal levels or -0.5 projection.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
410 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (By this time we are already in position to ride the actual move after the fake breakout, price will move faster and cleaner also allowing you to build a larger position towards the higher projections of the range and compound on the winners.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
